# NetSurf 3DS — Main Rule

## Project

Homebrew 3DS port of NetSurf using the **framebuffer** frontend. Targets ARM via devkitPro (libctru, 3DS portlibs). Output binary: `nsfb.3dsx`.

## Build after every change (required)

After **every** code change, run a build and fix any errors before continuing or reporting done.

From the repo root:

```bash
export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$(pwd)/inst-framebuffer/lib/pkgconfig:/opt/devkitpro/portlibs/3ds/lib/pkgconfig:${PKG_CONFIG_PATH}"
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/bison/bin:/opt/devkitpro/devkitARM/bin:/opt/devkitpro/tools/bin:${PATH}"
make --directory=netsurf PREFIX="$(pwd)/inst-framebuffer" TARGET=framebuffer NOCIA=1 -j$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu 2>/dev/null || nproc) && cp netsurf/nsfb.3dsx nsfb.3dsx
```

If a dependency library changed (e.g. `libnsfb/`), rebuild and install it first:

```bash
make --directory=libnsfb HOST=arm-none-eabi install PREFIX="$(pwd)/inst-framebuffer"
```

For a full clean rebuild: `make clean && make`.

- Treat compile warnings in changed code seriously; fix new ones you introduce.
- Do not assume the build passes — always run it and report the result.
- Deploy only when asked: `make deploy` (set `THREE_DS_IP` if needed).

## Where to edit

| Area | Path |
|------|------|
| 3DS UI, input, scrolling, zoom | `netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/gui.c` |
| Menus / settings overlay | `netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/app_menu.c` |
| Framebuffer frontend | `netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/` |
| SDL / 3DS surface & HID | `libnsfb/src/surface/sdl.c` |
| Top-level build | `Makefile` |

Wrap 3DS-only code in `#ifdef __3DS__` … `#endif`. Follow existing patterns (e.g. `fb_3ds_poll_*` helpers, `widget_set_scroll`).

## Coding

- Minimize scope — smallest correct diff, no unrelated changes.
- Match surrounding C style, naming, and abstractions.
- Only add comments for non-obvious logic.
- Do not commit, push, or open PRs unless explicitly asked.
